# Vulnerabilities accepted with justification. Each entry names where the
# finding comes from, why it is not reachable from FLITS, and what would make it
# actionable again. Review these whenever the base image or pip is bumped.

# GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964 - msgpack out-of-bounds read on Unpacker reuse.
# CVE-2025-47273      - setuptools path traversal in PackageIndex.
# CVE-2026-97687      - urllib3 traffic interception via HTTPS proxy TLS
#                       configuration override.
# CVE-2026-97689      - urllib3 denial of service via unbounded memory
#                       allocation in the chunk parser.
#
# All are reported against copies vendored inside pip itself
# (site-packages/pip/_vendor/vendor.txt pins msgpack==1.1.2,
# setuptools==70.3.0 and urllib3==2.7.0, still true of pip 26.2.2). The
# installed top-level msgpack and setuptools are current -- the Dockerfile
# floors them and asserts the result -- and the image installs no top-level
# urllib3 at all. pip's private copies cannot be upgraded independently of pip,
# and pip is already at the latest release.
#
# None is reachable from FLITS: the vendored code runs only when pip itself
# installs packages, which does not happen at runtime. Drop these entries once
# a pip release ships updated vendored versions.
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
CVE-2025-47273
CVE-2026-97687
CVE-2026-97689

# CVE-2026-114613 - msgpack C-extension memory leak / parser reference handling.
# Trivy reports pip 26.2.2's vendored msgpack 1.1.2 from its vendor manifest.
# That pip wheel contains no _cmsgpack extension: both Unpacker and unpackb
# resolve to pip._vendor.msgpack.fallback. The upstream advisory identifies
# the C extension as affected and reports the Python fallback unaffected:
# https://github.com/msgpack/msgpack-python/security/advisories/GHSA-j586-36cw-2gc2
# The separately installed msgpack is protected by an asserted >=1.2.3 floor
# in Dockerfile and docker/verify_security_floors.py. Recheck this exception
# when pip changes its vendored implementation or updates msgpack.
CVE-2026-114613
